sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant C as SSE client
    participant H as HTTP handler
    participant F as stream fanout hub
    participant R as Redis
    C->>H: GET offset and live=sse
    H->>H: authorize · parse offset and cursor · choose event encoding
    H->>F: reserve existing hub or prepare a new one
    F->>R: SUBSCRIBE and confirm for a new hub
    H->>R: atomic first bounded page after registration
    H->>F: seed hub tail and incarnation from that page
    F-->>H: hub ready without an attach reread
    H->>R: continue catch-up to the fixed page tail
    H-->>C: data then control offset
    H->>F: attach watcher at sent offset
    Note over H,F: no gap between catch-up and live delivery
    R-->>F: append wake hint
    F->>R: read new durable suffix once
    F-->>H: shared immutable data event
    H-->>C: shared data then client control
    Note over C,H: the client persists only complete control offsets for resume
